description:
## What

1. Delete all three old templates
2. Create mcp-server.subdomain.conf.j2 — clean subdomain template matching the arcane.subdomain.conf gold standard
3. Create mcp-server.subfolder.conf.j2 — subfolder variant (location block only, no server block)

## Context

### Gold Standard Pattern (from arcane.subdomain.conf)

The new subdomain template must generate configs that look like arcane.subdomain.conf:

**Server block structure:**
```
server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    listen [::]:443 ssl;
    server_name {{ server_name }};
    include /config/nginx/ssl.conf;
    client_max_body_size 0;

    # Upstream vars
    set $upstream_app "{{ upstream_app }}";
    set $upstream_port "{{ upstream_port }}";
    set $upstream_proto "{{ upstream_proto }}";
    set $mcp_upstream_app "{{ mcp_upstream_app }}";
    set $mcp_upstream_port "{{ mcp_upstream_port }}";
    set $mcp_upstream_proto "{{ mcp_upstream_proto }}";

    # DNS rebinding protection
    set $origin_valid 0;
    if ($http_origin = "") { set $origin_valid 1; }
    if ($http_origin = "https://$server_name") { set $origin_valid 1; }
    if ($http_origin ~ "^https://(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1)(:[0-9]+)?$") { set $origin_valid 1; }
    if ($http_origin ~ "^https://(.*.)?anthropic\.com$") { set $origin_valid 1; }
    if ($http_origin ~ "^https://(.*.)?claude\.ai$") { set $origin_valid 1; }

    # MCP security headers
    add_header X-MCP-Version "2025-06-18" always;
    add_header Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin" always;

    {% if auth_method != "none" %}
    include /config/nginx/{{ auth_method }}-server.conf;
    {% endif %}

    # All OAuth endpoints (/_oauth_verify, /.well-known/*, /token, /authorize, etc.)
    include /config/nginx/oauth.conf;

    location /mcp {
        if ($origin_valid = 0) { return 403 ...; }
        auth_request /_oauth_verify;
        auth_request_set $auth_status $upstream_status;
        include /config/nginx/mcp.conf;
        proxy_max_temp_file_size 0;
        chunked_transfer_encoding on;
        proxy_set_header Connection '';
        proxy_set_header MCP-Protocol-Version $http_mcp_protocol_version;
        proxy_set_header Mcp-Session-Id $http_mcp_session_id;
        proxy_set_header Accept $http_accept;
        proxy_connect_timeout 240s;
        proxy_send_timeout 86400s;
        proxy_read_timeout 86400s;
        add_header Cache-Control "no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate" always;
        # CORS headers + OPTIONS preflight handling
        proxy_pass $mcp_upstream_proto://$mcp_upstream_app:$mcp_upstream_port;
    }

    location /health {
        include /config/nginx/mcp.conf;
        proxy_connect_timeout 5s;
        proxy_send_timeout 10s;
        proxy_read_timeout 10s;
        add_header Cache-Control "no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate" always;
        proxy_pass $upstream_proto://$upstream_app:$upstream_port;
    }

    location ~* ^/(session|sessions) {
        auth_request /_oauth_verify;
        auth_request_set $auth_status $upstream_status;
        include /config/nginx/resolver.conf;
        include /config/nginx/proxy.conf;
        proxy_set_header MCP-Protocol-Version $http_mcp_protocol_version;
        proxy_set_header Mcp-Session-Id $http_mcp_session_id;
        add_header Cache-Control "no-store" always;
        proxy_pass $mcp_upstream_proto://$mcp_upstream_app:$mcp_upstream_port;
    }

    location / {
        {% if auth_method != "none" %}
        include /config/nginx/{{ auth_method }}-location.conf;
        {% endif %}
        include /config/nginx/resolver.conf;
        include /config/nginx/proxy.conf;
        proxy_pass $upstream_proto://$upstream_app:$upstream_port;
    }
}
```

### Subfolder Template

The subfolder template is a location block variant — NO server block, NO ssl, NO well-known OAuth endpoints (those can't live under a subfolder). It provides:
- /mcp location with OAuth auth_request
- /health location
- The root subfolder location with auth_method

Note: oauth.conf cannot be included in a subfolder template since it contains server-level OAuth discovery endpoints. The subfolder template's /mcp gets OAuth protection via auth_request /_oauth_verify but the /_oauth_verify location must exist in the parent server block.

### Template Variables

Required:
- service_name, server_name, upstream_app, upstream_port, upstream_proto
- mcp_upstream_app, mcp_upstream_port, mcp_upstream_proto (default to upstream_* values)
- auth_method (default: authelia)
- enable_quic (default: false)

## Decisions

### Locked
- auth_method controls Authelia (server + location level) on / — defaults to authelia
- /mcp is ALWAYS protected by auth_request /_oauth_verify (OAuth) regardless of auth_method
- oauth.conf is included at server level (contains all OAuth location blocks)
- Template names: mcp-server.subdomain.conf.j2 and mcp-server.subfolder.conf.j2
- Delete: mcp_location_block.j2, swag-compliant-mcp-subdomain.conf.j2, swag-compliant-mcp-subfolder.conf.j2

### Discretion
- Whether to add QUIC support block ({% if enable_quic %}) — include it for completeness
- Comment style and density — match SWAG sample config style (minimal, purposeful)

## Testing

- [ ] Template renders without Jinja2 errors for all variable combinations
- [ ] auth_method=authelia: includes authelia-server.conf and authelia-location.conf
- [ ] auth_method=none: no authelia includes
- [ ] mcp_upstream_app differs from upstream_app: /mcp routes to different upstream
- [ ] Generated config passes nginx -t syntax check
- [ ] /mcp location always has auth_request /_oauth_verify
- [ ] oauth.conf include is always present in subdomain template

## Validation

- [ ] templates/mcp-server.subdomain.conf.j2 exists
- [ ] templates/mcp-server.subfolder.conf.j2 exists
- [ ] Old templates deleted (mcp_location_block.j2, swag-compliant-*.conf.j2)
- [ ] Generated subdomain config matches arcane.subdomain.conf structure

## Files

- /home/jmagar/code/swag-mcp/templates/mcp-server.subdomain.conf.j2 (create)
- /home/jmagar/code/swag-mcp/templates/mcp-server.subfolder.conf.j2 (create)
- /home/jmagar/code/swag-mcp/templates/mcp_location_block.j2 (delete)
- /home/jmagar/code/swag-mcp/templates/swag-compliant-mcp-subdomain.conf.j2 (delete)
- /home/jmagar/code/swag-mcp/templates/swag-compliant-mcp-subfolder.conf.j2 (delete)
- /home/jmagar/code/swag-mcp/templates/CLAUDE.md (update template inventory)

## Dependencies

- swag-mcp-r4g.1 (oauth.conf must exist to know what to reference)

